cross-domain bridges (a tool in one domain that speaks another's port — never a copy of the other domain):
    - image.image-source ↔ video.frame-grab
    - image.layer-stack ↔ image-source, mask-brush
    - image.curves ↔ music.lfo
    - image.color-grade ↔ video.video-grade
    - image.mask-brush ↔ layer-stack, selection
    - image.selection ↔ mask-brush
    - image.grain-texture ↔ music.fx-haunt
    - image.text-layer ↔ ui.style-tokens
    - video.clip-source ↔ music.song-recorder
    - video.video-timeline ↔ music.timeline, music.transport
    - video.beat-cut ↔ music.pads, music.bass-drop-builder
    - video.transition ↔ music.lfo
    - video.video-grade ↔ image.color-grade
    - video.text-overlay ↔ music.timeline
    - video.frame-grab ↔ image.image-source
    - video.video-export ↔ music.song-recorder
    - ui.text-block ↔ image.text-layer
    - ui.image-block ↔ image.image-export
    - ui.button ↔ agents.trigger-event
    - ui.interaction ↔ music.lfo
    - agents.trigger-event ↔ music.song-recorder, ui.button
    - agents.song-writer ↔ music.song-engine, music.song-recorder
rule: no domain is a monolith — a domain is only its tools; remove a tool's pack and only that tool is gone.
